[0.010345, "o", "\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\ncorro 0.7.0 on the zork backend\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[0.012542, "o", "\r\n\r\n[part 1 of 3]  The app builds its GUI tree, then records what it built\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nThe widget tree is corro's real GUI construction path, built against the\r\nin-memory model instead of a display. The record is written to a file,\r\nbecause it has to be taken while the tree is still live: the REPL adopts\r\nthe model on startup, after which all 98 nodes are gone.\r\n\r\n  $ echo quit | CORRO_ZORK_WALKTHROUGH=<file> ./target/debug/corro\r\n\r\n"]
[0.028745, "o", "corro 0.7.0 on the zork backend\r\n======================================================\r\n\r\nThe widget tree above this text is corro's real GUI tree,\r\nbuilt against an in-memory model instead of a display.\r\n\r\n"]
[0.02907, "o", "Widgets built: 98\r\n"]
[0.02934, "o", "  2 xBoxWidget, 2 xCanvas, 1 xEntry, 4 xLabel, 20 xMenu, 1 xScrolledWindow, 67 xSimpleAction, 1 xWindow\r\nWindow title: \"corro 0.7.0\"\r\nCursor at rest: R999999999C702\r\n"]
